THROWAWAY patch from the real-world memory spike of 2026-11-04, variant FNC: never merge.
It applies to 296ad44 (#559) with `patch -p1` or `git apply`.
A GET's prefetched head is served from its free-list buffer instead of a copy; the
buffer goes back to the list once, when the request's context ends or the state is discarded.

